-<p>Owns the common-first session boundary, physical producer/member/release records, source-owned transition execution and reference refresh. Retired-owner terminal APIs are separate from ordinary admission. A current physical inventory or controlled observation is not a human approval or a native runner certification.</p>
+<p>Owns the common-first session boundary, physical producer/member/release records, source-owned transition execution and reference refresh. Retired-owner terminal APIs are separate from ordinary admission. A current physical inventory or controlled observation is not a human approval or a native runner certification. Checks each registry object once, heals once, keeps source digests and prunes settled members, skips a registry lock that vanished during the closure walk, and treats a failed Windows directory fsync as a warning. A normally released writer that left the State settled no longer blocks the next close step, and a declined acceptance is routed back into a correction round.</p>
